name social-bias-frames-aggregated
# The set's README ("Aggregation"): the files "aggregated per post": for a post, the mean of whoTarget, intentYN,
# sexYN and offensiveYN over its annotations, the set of what was written as targetMinority, targetCategory and
# targetStereotype, each written as a JSON list ("To load the list of implications, use json.loads"), and
# hasBiasedImplication. A post has no HITId here: it is the text it is. What a row says of it, it says together.
# Each field states the relation the README words for it (see annotations.recipe), here over all the post's
# annotations: the mean of the answers, the set of the texts.
# hasBiasedImplication is computed by the README's own code from targetStereotype,
#   gDf["hasBiasedImplication"] = (gDf["targetStereotype"].apply(len) == 0).astype(int)
# (1 where the list is empty): the list is recorded, so the flag says nothing more and is read by nothing.
match SBIC.v2.agg.*.csv

tier row by \n
header
quoted
tier field by ,
part targetMinority by json
part targetCategory by json
part targetStereotype by json

thing row post
content post targetMinority targetCategory targetStereotype whoTarget intentYN sexYN offensiveYN dataSource
omit hasBiasedImplication
together row
# whoTarget: group vs. individual target;  intentYN: was the intent behind the statement to offend;
# sexYN: is the post a sexual or lewd reference;  offensiveYN: could the post be offensive to anyone;
# targetMinority: demographic group targeted;  targetCategory: high-level category of the demographic group(s)
# targeted;  targetStereotype: implied statement;  dataSource: source of the post
relation "group vs. individual target" whoTarget
relation "was the intent behind the statement to offend" intentYN
relation "is the post a sexual or lewd reference" sexYN
relation "could the post be offensive to anyone" offensiveYN
relation "demographic group targeted" targetMinority
relation "high-level category of the demographic group(s) targeted" targetCategory
relation "implied statement" targetStereotype
relation "source of the post" dataSource
attest row targetMinority targetCategory targetStereotype whoTarget intentYN sexYN offensiveYN dataSource
